Summary: Nice update to FSX, with lots of potential.
Before going on with the review, I have to make one thing very clear: I don't care much about hardcore simulation. All I want from a flight sim, is a relaxing experience. To be able to take off, get the plane on route, and admire the scenery. So, performance and good graphics are important to me.
So, I was on the fence about buying this, because of all the bad reviews. Then I thought "whatever, if it's a letdown like another recently released flight sim was, I'll ask for a refund." So I purchased it, installed, and launched the game. My first impression was weird. It has a very nice menu, with easy to find options and settings, but... It felt limited. Anyway, I started a free flight, selected an airport (my usual benchmarking airport for all flight sims I try) and began my comparison with FSX.
I was not disappointed. At all.
The graphics took a huge step forward. The scenery is way more detailed, a lot of nice effects were added, and the ground mesh has a much better resolution. The only bad thing here is that the shorelines are very straight (low resolution poligons), just like FSX. The water and weather could be better as well, but look better than FSX. All of this with a better overall performance. So, first impressions were good. Oh, and the graphics can be improved if you increase the LOD (by default, the LOD is very low, and distant terrain looks very bad). There is a topic explaining how to do that.
Other good stuff:
- The sounds are very good;
- Turbulence effects are more... Let's say, noticeable;
- Very nice interface, overall;
- Nice flight planner (yes, you can just select the starting airport without making a flight plan in free flight, contrary to what another reviewer said);
- Few planes, but all of them are VERY well made. More to come, for sure;
- Really, really cool license progression and missions, with flight hours logging;
- 64-bit means more ram is used, so a larger chunk of scenery is loaded, so less blurriness due to slow texture loading (nothing new here, other major FSs already do this);
Now, for the bad stuff... I really hope all of this changes over time:
- Limited weather selection: you can only choose some patterns, and can't change it during flight;
Ignore the section below, I was stupid and didn't find where to change the time. Still can't change it during the flight, though.
-----
- NO TIME OF DAY SELECTION! Some weather patterns are set in a certain time of day but, as the weather itself, you can't change it. I'm still not sure if the time passes normally or is fixed;
-----
Ignore the section above, I was stupid and didn't find where to change the time. Still can't change it during the flight, though.
- Few planes, but as I mentioned, more are on the way;
- Incompatibility with most fsx add-ons;
- Problems when alt+tabbing;
- Could use some better optimization. I don't usually get low frame rates, but when taking off or landing at a busy and detailed airport, on a detailed city, it can drop a lot. My system is quite dated, though;
So, overall, I would recomend it. For me, it provided the exact experience I was looking for, and still have a lot of potential to become better and better. If you liked FSX but never quite got to playing Steam Edition because it felt too dated, get this. But if you are searching for a more hardcore experience, wait a bit and see how it develops.
